    "description": {
      "value": "<p><em>“This happened. It matters. Act accordingly.”</em></p><p>When a significant action succeeds or fails, you may establish a <strong>Precedent</strong> tied to a creature, location, faction, or concept. While active, similar future actions reroll the lowest die if aligned with the precedent, or suffer disadvantage if they violate it. You are not forcing outcomes—you are making contradiction expensive.</p><p><strong>Precedent is probability gravity, not mind control.</strong></p>",
